course: dictionary
lesson: 1769
title: Words for people who lead church services
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A clergyman is a man who leads religious services, such as a priest, minister, vicar or rabbi. A woman who does the same job is a clergywoman. Both are members of the clergy.
explain: Use the words around clergyman to find its meaning. «The village clergyman rang the bell and everyone walked into the church.» The bell and the church are clues: a clergyman leads services in a place like that.
explain: Clergyman is often used in history and stories, and at weddings and funerals. Vicar, priest, pastor and minister are related words with similar meanings, so you can use them to help you remember.
fact: A clergyman is a man who leads religious services.
fact: A clergywoman does the same job, but she is a woman.
fact: The plural of clergyman is clergymen.
fact: «A man of the cloth» means a priest or clergyman, someone whose job is to lead a church.
fact: Member of the clergy is a neutral phrase, so it can be used for any person in this job.
fact: Related words: vicar, priest, pastor, minister, rabbi.
exercise: «The village clergyman rang the bell before the service.» Who leads the service? | The mayor's dog | The baker | *The clergyman | The school cook
exercise: What is the plural of clergyman? | *clergymen | clergymans | clergymanes | clergyman's
exercise: What does «member of the clergy» mean? | *Someone who leads religious services | Someone who cleans the church | A choir singer only | A visitor who sits at the back
test: «A man of the cloth» means what? | *A priest or clergyman, someone who leads a church | A soldier | A man who sells cloth at the market | A tailor who sews robes
test: Which word means a woman who does the same job as a clergyman? | Clergyday | Clergyboy | *Clergywoman | Clergyhouse
exam: «At the wedding, the clergyman smiled and read the vows.» Who is leading the wedding? | *The clergyman | The taxi driver | The wedding cake | The bride's cat
